  nodeGroups?: [ 
    {
      fileSystemMountEnabled?: boolean(name='FileSystemMountEnabled', description='Specifies whether file system mounting is supported.', example='false'),
      hyperNodes?: [ 
        {
          dataDisk?: [ 
            {
              burstingEnabled?: boolean(name='BurstingEnabled', description='Specifies whether to enable the burstable performance feature.', example='true'),
              category?: string(name='Category', description='The disk category. Valid values:

- cloud_essd: ESSD.', example='cloud_essd'),
              deleteWithNode?: boolean(name='DeleteWithNode', description='Specifies whether to release the data cloud disk when the node is released.', example='true'),
              device?: string(name='Device', description='The device name of the data cloud disk. This parameter is used only in full image scenarios. You can use this parameter to set the device name of the data cloud disk to match the source data cloud disk in the full image, and modify the properties of the corresponding data cloud disk. For non-full image scaling, the Device parameter is set by the system by default. When you use a full image for scaling:

- Regardless of whether the data cloud disk parameters are explicitly set, the system restores the data cloud disks from the source image for the user. The content is consistent with the data cloud disks in the source image.
- If data cloud disks are explicitly specified but the Device parameter is not set, additional empty data cloud disks are created. The quantity and properties are specified by the user data cloud disk parameters.
- If the Device parameter of the explicitly specified data cloud disk does not match the Device parameter of the source image data cloud disk, additional empty data cloud disks are created. The quantity and properties are specified by the user data cloud disk parameters.
- If multiple data cloud disks and their Device parameters are explicitly specified, but all Device parameters point to the same device of a data cloud disk in the source image, only one of the specified data cloud disks matches and overwrites the source image data cloud disk by device. The other specified data cloud disks are silently discarded, and no additional empty data cloud disks are created.
- If the Device parameter of the explicitly specified data cloud disk matches the Device parameter of the source image data cloud disk, no additional empty data cloud disks are created. The user-specified data cloud disks correspond to the source image data cloud disks one by one through the device parameter. If the Size of the user-specified data cloud disk is smaller than the Size of the source image data cloud disk, the system returns HTTP status code 417 and the error message: Data disk Size can not be less than the image data disk snapshot size for Device \\\\"/dev/xvdb\\\\".
- The total number of data cloud disks mounted to the node (specified data cloud disks + data cloud disks restored from the image) cannot exceed 16 for standard cloud disk groups, and cannot exceed 4 when Cloud Paralleled File System (CPFS) is enabled.', example='/dev/xvdb'),
              encrypted?: boolean(name='Encrypted', description='Specifies whether to encrypt the data cloud disk. Valid values:
- true: The data cloud disk is encrypted.
- false: The data cloud disk is not encrypted.

Default value: false.


>Notice: When you use a shared encrypted image to create a cloud disk based on an encrypted snapshot, you must set the Encrypted request parameter of the cloud disk to true. This ensures that the created cloud disk is encrypted by using the key of the shared image recipient.</notice>', example='false'),
              KMSKeyId?: string(name='KMSKeyId', description='The KMS key ID of the data cloud disk.

If the Encrypted parameter is set to true but you do not specify KMSKeyId, the default key is used for encryption, and the KMSKeyId value is returned after the instance is created.
- If the cloud disk is created from a non-shared encrypted snapshot, the encryption key used for the snapshot is used by default.
- If the cloud disk is created from a shared encrypted snapshot, the service key is used by default.
- If the cloud disk is created in a region where account-level default encryption for Block Storage is enabled, the specified account-level key is used by default.
- In other cases, the service key is used by default.', example='57e27f4a-f60f-4e8f-bbae-6c042e9a5ed6'),
              performanceLevel?: string(name='PerformanceLevel', description='The performance level of the ESSD used as the data cloud disk. Valid values:
- PL0: The cloud disk can deliver up to 10,000 random read/write IOPS.
- PL1: The cloud disk can deliver up to 50,000 random read/write IOPS.
- PL2: The cloud disk can deliver up to 100,000 random read/write IOPS.
- PL3: The cloud disk can deliver up to 1,000,000 random read/write IOPS.

Default value: PL1.', example='PL0'),
              provisionedIops?: long(name='ProvisionedIops', description='The provisioned read and write IOPS for the ESSD AutoPL cloud disk.', example='10000'),
              size?: int32(name='Size', description='The size of the cloud disk. Unit: GiB.', example='180'),
            }
          ](name='DataDisk', description='The list of data cloud disks.'),
          hostname?: string(name='Hostname', description='The hostname.', example='q25b01265.cloud.ng152'),
          hyperNodeId?: string(name='HyperNodeId', description='The hypernode ID.', example='e01-dw72u2c23jk'),
          loginPassword?: string(name='LoginPassword', description='The logon password.', example='aaadddddfdsfdsfsdffd'),
          vSwitchId?: string(name='VSwitchId', description='The vSwitch ID.', example='vsw-bp1xn9iq3s3p8218c4qu4'),
          vpcId?: string(name='VpcId', description='The VPC ID.', example='vpc-uf689skpx56nk7yfw0jhy'),
        }
      ](name='HyperNodes', description='The list of hypernodes.'),
      imageId?: string(name='ImageId', description='The image ID.', example='i190297201634099844192'),
      keyPairName?: string(name='KeyPairName', description='The name of the key pair.', example='test-keypair'),
      loginPassword?: string(name='LoginPassword', description='The logon password.', example='Password'),
      machineType?: string(name='MachineType', description='The machine type.', example='efg1.nvga1'),
      nodeGroupDescription?: string(name='NodeGroupDescription', description='The description of the node group.', example='Default node group'),
      nodeGroupName?: string(name='NodeGroupName', description='The name of the node group.', example='emr-default'),
      nodes?: [ 
        {
          dataDisk?: [ 
            {
              burstingEnabled?: boolean(name='BurstingEnabled', description='Specifies whether to enable the burstable performance feature.', example='false'),
              category?: string(name='Category', description='The category.', example='cloud_essd'),
              deleteWithNode?: boolean(name='DeleteWithNode', description='Specifies whether to release the data cloud disk when the node is released.', example='true'),
              device?: string(name='Device', description='The device name of the data cloud disk. This parameter is used only in full image scenarios. You can use this parameter to set the device name of the data cloud disk to match the source data cloud disk in the full image, and modify the properties of the corresponding data cloud disk. For non-full image scaling, the Device parameter is set by the system by default. When you use a full image for scaling:

- Regardless of whether the data cloud disk parameters are explicitly set, the system restores the data cloud disks from the source image for the user. The content is consistent with the data cloud disks in the source image.
- If data cloud disks are explicitly specified but the Device parameter is not set, additional empty data cloud disks are created. The quantity and properties are specified by the user data cloud disk parameters.
- If the Device parameter of the explicitly specified data cloud disk does not match the Device parameter of the source image data cloud disk, additional empty data cloud disks are created. The quantity and properties are specified by the user data cloud disk parameters.
- If multiple data cloud disks and their Device parameters are explicitly specified, but all Device parameters point to the same device of a data cloud disk in the source image, only one of the specified data cloud disks matches and overwrites the source image data cloud disk by device. The other specified data cloud disks are silently discarded, and no additional empty data cloud disks are created.
- If the Device parameter of the explicitly specified data cloud disk matches the Device parameter of the source image data cloud disk, no additional empty data cloud disks are created. The user-specified data cloud disks correspond to the source image data cloud disks one by one through the device parameter. If the Size of the user-specified data cloud disk is smaller than the Size of the source image data cloud disk, the system returns HTTP status code 417 and the error message: Data disk Size can not be less than the image data disk snapshot size for Device \\\\"/dev/xvdb\\\\".
- The total number of data cloud disks mounted to the node (specified data cloud disks + data cloud disks restored from the image) cannot exceed 16 for standard cloud disk groups, and cannot exceed 4 when Cloud Paralleled File System (CPFS) is enabled.', example='/dev/xvdb'),
              encrypted?: boolean(name='Encrypted', description='Specifies whether to encrypt the data cloud disk. Valid values:
- true: The data cloud disk is encrypted.
- false: The data cloud disk is not encrypted.

